course: dictionary
lesson: 14411
title: Overfed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix over- often means too much, as in overfull, overcooked and overeat. Overfed is the past form of the verb overfeed, which means to feed something too much. So overfed means given too much food, more than is healthy.
explain: «The vet said the cat was overfed and needs smaller meals.» The word overfed tells you the cat had too much food. The vet's worry shows that too much food is not good for it. Check your meaning: "The cat was given too much food" still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Overfed can also describe something. «The overfed goldfish floated sleepily near the top of the tank.» Here overfed comes before the noun goldfish, so it tells us about the fish. Watch out: fed means given food, well fed means given enough food, and overfed means given too much.
fact: The prefix over- at the start of a word often means too much: overfed, overheated, overcooked.
fact: Overfeed is the verb, as in «They overfed the fish», so overfed is its past form.
fact: «Overfed» means given too much food, more than is healthy.
fact: Animals such as fish, dogs and cats can be harmed by too much food.
fact: In stories, an overfed animal is often shown as fat and lazy.
exercise: «The vet said the cat was overfed.» What does overfed mean? | Given too little food | *Given too much food | Given food that was too cold | Given a new bowl
exercise: «The overfed fish looked round and lazy.» Find and copy the word that tells us the fish had too much food. | *overfed | lazy | round | looked
exercise: Mum says, «Do not overfeed the dog, it will get sick.» What does overfeed mean? | *To give the dog too much food | To walk the dog every day | To wash the dog's bowl | To give the dog too little food
test: Which word is the past form of overfeed? | overfeeder | overfeeds | *overfed | overfeeding
test: Which sentence tells us the dog was given too much food? | *The dog was overfed at every meal | The dog was well fed and happy | The dog was lost in the park | The dog was taken for a walk
exam: «The hamster was overfed, so it became too fat to run on its wheel.» What does overfed mean in this sentence? | *It means given too much food, so the hamster got too fat | It means very hungry | It means given a new wheel | It means well fed and healthy
